data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/dispatch_dev_1.md\", \"content\": \"Task: implement the \\\"greet, tested\\\" feature in the subject repo, on your own branch.\\n\\nRequirements (all must be met):\\n\\n1. Create `src/greet.py` with a function `greet(name)` that returns the string\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`).\\n2. Create `tests/test_greet.py` with unit tests covering:\\n   - a normal name (e.g. asserts `greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`)\\n   - the empty string (asserts `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`)\\n3. Verify locally, from the repo root, that:\\n     python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n   exits 0 (all tests pass).\\n4. Commit your work to your own branch.\\n\\nIn your reply, state clearly: the exact command you ran to verify, its exit\\ncode, and confirm the commit is on your branch. Tell the truth about any\\nfailures or things you could not verify.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

